          "focus": "Link clauses, phrases, and sentences in accordance with Standard English punctuation and boundary conventions",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 1 · Q10",
          "passageTitle": "Boundaries — Q10",
          "passage": "In Puerto Rico, it is not unusual for a city or town to be known by a nickname that corresponds to one of its notable features, like landscape, climate, famous residents, or chief exports. For example, the Puerto Rican Municipality of Arecibo has also been called \"the villa of Captain Correa,\" a nickname that alludes to what the area is well ______ Antonio de Correa, the 17th-century army captain who once defended the town.",
